Ladybird resolves the percentage margins of an absolutely positioned
box against the inline size of its containing block, in both axes,
whether or not the box is sized as a replaced element. Both Blink’s
ComputeMarginsFor() and Gecko’s SizeComputationInput::ComputeMargin()
resolve all four margins against a single basis, the inline size of the
containing block. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit
26.5: All three put an image, a canvas, a checkbox, and a text input
with a 10% margin in a 300x50 containing block at 30,30.
